\title{ledgr condition classes}
\description{
ledgr uses stable top-level condition classes for public cost-model,
timing-model, execution-window, saved-sweep, and retained-series failures.
User tests should assert on these classes instead of parsing message text.
}
\section{Cost and timing classes}{

\code{ledgr_cost_model_unspecified} is raised when a public execution entry point
omits \code{cost_model} or supplies \code{NULL}. Use \code{\link[=ledgr_cost_zero]{ledgr_cost_zero()}} for explicit
zero-cost execution.

\code{ledgr_invalid_cost_model} is raised for invalid cost-model objects,
malformed cost plans, unsupported cost-plan steps, or invalid cost-model
constructor arguments.

\code{ledgr_invalid_cost_chain_order} is raised when a cost chain violates the
required order: price-transform steps before explicit-fee steps.

\code{ledgr_invalid_timing_model} is raised for non-ledgr timing-model objects or
malformed ledgr timing-model payloads.
}

\section{Fill seam classes}{

\code{ledgr_invalid_fill_proposal} and \code{ledgr_invalid_fill_context} are raised at
the internal proposal/resolver seam when a cost resolver receives the wrong
object shape. They are stable top-level classes for tests that exercise that
seam directly.
}

\section{Execution window classes}{

\code{ledgr_run_window_too_short} is raised when a run window contains fewer than
two executable pulses. Next-bar fill semantics require a decision pulse and a
later execution pulse.
}

\section{Accounting classes}{

\code{ledgr_invalid_lot_fill} is raised when the lot-accounting layer receives an
invalid fill side, quantity, price, fee, or instrument id. Invalid lot input
fails closed because the ledger event stream and lot state must not diverge.
}

\section{Snapshot hash classes}{

\code{ledgr_snapshot_hash_invalid_timestamp} is raised when snapshot hashing sees
a non-POSIXct \code{ts_utc} representation. Snapshot hashes fail closed on driver
timestamp representation drift instead of silently re-keying sealed data.

\code{ledgr_snapshot_hash_rule_unsupported} is raised when a snapshot does not
carry the current content-hash rule.
\code{ledgr_snapshot_hash_order_invalid} is raised when source rows are not in
the bytewise order required by the current snapshot-hash rule.

\code{ledgr_fact_civil_date_unresolved} is raised when a fact Date does not map
to exactly one declared open venue session. \code{ledgr_session_boundary_unresolved}
applies the same refusal to an availability-aware execution boundary.
\code{ledgr_corporate_action_clock_missing} is raised, at its knowledge cutoff,
for a knowable corporate action with neither entitlement nor effective time.
\code{ledgr_corporate_action_entitlement_missing} is raised, at the pulse it would
act on and in every execution mode, for a complete \code{ordinary_cash_dividend},
\code{cash_acquisition}, \code{stock_acquisition}, \code{mixed_acquisition} or \code{spin_off}
row with an effective clock but no entitlement clock; it carries the fact and instrument IDs, the subtype and
the effective and knowledge clocks, and the user supplies the entitlement
time.
\code{ledgr_invalid_history_policy} is raised for malformed history-policy
constructor arguments or a non-current policy object.
\code{ledgr_history_identity_mismatch} and \code{ledgr_precomputed_history_mismatch}
refuse non-current causal-history identity in configs and precomputed data.
\code{ledgr_invalid_history_substrate} refuses a substrate owned by a different
snapshot, policy, universe, range or representation version.
\code{ledgr_history_duplicate_bar}, \code{ledgr_history_outside_axis} and
\code{ledgr_history_unknown_instrument} refuse ambiguous or out-of-domain history
preparation and reads. \code{ledgr_history_segment_missing} refuses an invalid
internal segment plane rather than returning fabricated state.
\code{ledgr_history_segment_limit_exceeded} reports an instrument, fact family,
fact count, segment count, ratio and limit when causal preparation exceeds
its declared bound. \code{ledgr_fact_knowledge_missing} refuses, before any run,
sweep, precompute, walk-forward or inspection side effect, a snapshot whose
membership, trading-status or lifetime facts lack a knowledge time.
\code{ledgr_invalid_history_treatment} and
\code{ledgr_invalid_history_field} refuse malformed treatment evidence or an
unsupported bar field. \code{ledgr_history_unavailable} refuses a history read
from a dense or snapshot-and-universe pulse context, which has no causal
history. \code{ledgr_invalid_history_request} refuses malformed
\code{\link[=ledgr_history_frame]{ledgr_history_frame()}} and \code{\link[=ledgr_history_matrix]{ledgr_history_matrix()}} request arguments,
including a missing required \code{lookback}, and \code{ledgr_invalid_history_result}
refuses a matrix,
metadata, weights or sufficiency query on a value that is not, or no longer
matches, a \code{ledgr_history} result. \code{ledgr_weight_alignment_mismatch}
refuses \code{\link[=ledgr_align_weights]{ledgr_align_weights()}} solver output whose length, names or shape
do not match the history result's included instruments.
\code{ledgr_pulse_snapshot_availability_required} refuses experiment-derived
\code{\link[=ledgr_pulse_snapshot]{ledgr_pulse_snapshot()}} inspection of a dense experiment, and
\code{ledgr_pulse_inspection_stopped} refuses an inspection cutoff whose
observe-and-settle stage stops before the strategy context is built.
\code{ledgr_staged_history_mismatch} refuses a worker task
before candidate execution when its staged immutable input is absent or has
a different identity.
}

\section{Store-format classes}{

\code{ledgr_store_rebuild_required} is raised when a persistent store is older,
newer, unmarked, malformed, or carries a format fingerprint different from
this ledgr build. Before the first CRAN release ledgr does not migrate old
stores: rebuild them with the current package.
}

\section{Availability classes}{

\code{ledgr_invalid_valuation_policy} is raised for malformed stale-valuation
policies or constructor arguments.

\code{ledgr_availability_inactive} is raised when a membership-universe rule is
requested without the fact families needed to activate availability-aware
execution.

\code{ledgr_availability_sessions_required} is raised when availability-aware
execution lacks a complete session calendar.

\code{ledgr_backtest_availability_unsupported} is raised when \code{ledgr_backtest()}
receives a snapshot that declares point-in-time facts; use
\code{ledgr_experiment()} and \code{ledgr_run()}.

\code{ledgr_promote_identity_mismatch} is a warning raised when a promoted
candidate's recorded identities differ from the promoting experiment's.

\code{ledgr_sessions_incomplete} is raised when the declared session calendar
does not cover the requested start and end of a run, sweep, run window or
walk-forward fold.

\code{ledgr_membership_universe_not_found} is raised when a membership-universe
rule names a universe that is not declared by the snapshot.

\code{ledgr_compiled_availability_unsupported} is raised before execution when
availability-aware execution is combined with the compiled spot-FIFO path.

\code{ledgr_policy_schema_mismatch} is raised when a config or stored run carries
a non-current corporate-action or valuation policy schema. Current stores
carry schema 2; ledgr does not infer, migrate, or reinterpret older policy
records.

\code{ledgr_strategy_provenance_missing} is raised when a current run row exists
but its required strategy-provenance row is absent.

\code{ledgr_session_time_ambiguous} and \code{ledgr_session_time_nonexistent} are
raised when a local session wall time resolves to multiple UTC instants or
no UTC instant. Supply an explicit POSIXct instant to disambiguate a real
fall-back time.

\code{ledgr_fact_ambiguous_membership_shape} and
\code{ledgr_fact_invalid_membership_list} are raised for mixed row/list
membership input or malformed constituent lists.

\code{ledgr_facts_inspection_invalid_args} is raised for incompatible history or
resolution arguments. \code{ledgr_facts_scope_not_found} is raised when the
requested family and scope are not declared. Snapshot inspection raises
\code{ledgr_facts_snapshot_not_sealed} or
\code{ledgr_facts_snapshot_hash_mismatch} before returning evidence from an
unsealed or corrupted artifact.

\code{ledgr_session_adapter_invalid} and \code{ledgr_session_override_invalid} are
raised for malformed qlcal adapter inputs or replacement rows.

\code{ledgr_indicator_gap_parity} is raised when a custom bounded indicator's
\code{fn} on its window disagrees with its \code{series_fn} value beyond the declared
tolerance at a sampled causality position; its fields name the feature,
instrument and session. \code{ledgr_feature_lookahead_detected} is raised when a
feature recomputed from the history ending at a sampled session differs
from its prepared value; its fields name the feature, instrument and
session and carry both values.

\code{ledgr_invalid_indicator_declaration} (parent \code{ledgr_invalid_args}) is
raised for an invalid indicator history class, required-field set or
tolerance. \code{ledgr_indicator_history_contradiction} is its subclass for
contradictory declarations: a strict window declared history-dependent, a
tolerance without a bounded \code{fn}/\code{series_fn} pair, or a registered TTR form
declared against its catalogue row.

\code{ledgr_invalid_strategy_state} is raised when availability-aware asset state
is not a named list keyed only by instruments on the current public axis.

\code{ledgr_target_sizing_unavailable} is raised when an availability-aware
rebalance helper needs a permissible mark it cannot obtain: to reserve the
exposure of a preserved holding, or to keep a held member that has no
current close. A member without a current close is otherwise skipped for
that rebalance and recorded, not an error.

\code{ledgr_restricted_target} and \code{ledgr_nonmember_exposure_increase} are raised
when availability-aware strategy output violates the decision-time target
contract. \code{ledgr_post_risk_inadmissible} is raised when a risk step does not
preserve or reduce the strategy target. These conditions carry the affected
instrument IDs.

\code{ledgr_short_exposure_unsupported} is raised before fill acceptance when an
availability-aware target would open or enlarge short exposure. Existing
short quantities may be held or reduced; this does not define short-account
financing.

\code{ledgr_affordability_reconciliation_failed} is raised when recorded active
cash diverges from the bounded-affordability virtual ledger beyond the
engine's fixed tolerance.

\code{ledgr_run_terminal_evidence_invalid} is raised when persisted terminal
completion evidence is malformed, disagrees with the run calendar or stored
status, or does not match the finalized equity prefix and stop diagnostic.

\code{ledgr_run_explanation_unavailable} is raised when a run has no retained
decision trace for the requested instrument and timestamp. ledgr does not
infer the missing intent from current strategy code or other artifacts.
}

\section{Saved sweep classes}{

\code{ledgr_invalid_sweep_id} is raised when a saved sweep id is not a non-empty,
non-whitespace ASCII character scalar of at most 256 bytes.

\code{ledgr_sweep_id_exists} is raised when \code{ledgr_sweep_save()} would overwrite
an existing saved sweep id.

\code{ledgr_sweep_not_found} is raised when \code{ledgr_sweep_open()} is called with
a structurally valid saved sweep id that is not present in the experiment
store.

\code{ledgr_sweep_snapshot_not_found} is raised when a saved sweep's snapshot is
not present in the provided experiment store.

\code{ledgr_sweep_snapshot_hash_mismatch} is raised when the snapshot id exists
but its hash differs from the hash stored on the saved sweep.

\code{ledgr_sweep_schema_incompatible} is raised when saved sweep tables,
columns, or artifact schema versions are not compatible with the current
ledgr version.

\code{ledgr_invalid_sweep_retention} is raised when \code{ledgr_sweep_retention()} or
\code{ledgr_sweep(..., retain = )} receives an invalid retention policy.

\code{ledgr_sweep_returns_unretained} is raised when callers ask for retained
return rows from a scalar-only sweep.

\code{ledgr_sweep_returns_candidate_not_found} is raised when retained returns are
requested for an unknown \code{candidate_id}.

\code{ledgr_sweep_returns_candidate_not_completed} is raised when retained
returns are requested for a failed candidate or for a completed candidate
whose retained rows are missing.

\code{ledgr_sweep_returns_first_row_invalid} is raised when retained return rows
do not carry the required structural first-row \code{NA_real_} period return.

\code{ledgr_sweep_returns_incomplete_panel} is raised when callers request a
complete retained-return panel but selected completed candidates do not share
one common timestamp grid after first-row handling.
\code{ledgr_validation_pbo_incomplete_panel} is a compatibility alias on the same
condition for future PBO/CSCV adapters.

\code{ledgr_sweep_trades_unretained} is raised when callers ask for retained
closed-trade evidence from a sweep that did not opt into trade retention.

\code{ledgr_sweep_trades_candidate_not_found} is raised when retained trades are
requested for an unknown \code{candidate_id}.

\code{ledgr_sweep_trades_candidate_not_completed} is raised when retained trades
are requested for a failed candidate.

\code{ledgr_sweep_trades_candidate_not_retained} is raised when retained trades
are missing for a completed candidate that reports closed trades.

\code{ledgr_incomplete_sweep_candidate} is raised when candidate extraction is
requested for an \code{INCOMPLETE} sweep row. \code{ledgr_promote_incomplete_candidate}
is raised when promotion receives an incomplete candidate. Incomplete
prefixes remain evidence and never become executable candidates.

\code{ledgr_validation_pbo_invalid_s} is raised when a PBO/CSCV request supplies
an invalid \code{S} subset count.

\code{ledgr_validation_pbo_too_few_candidates} is raised when PBO/CSCV has fewer
than two completed candidates.

\code{ledgr_validation_pbo_too_few_observations} is raised when PBO/CSCV has too
few post-first-row observations for the requested partitioning.

\code{ledgr_validation_pbo_invalid_metric} is raised when a PBO/CSCV metric is not
callable or does not return one finite numeric score per candidate.

\code{ledgr_validation_pbo_invalid_panel} is raised when PBO/CSCV receives a
non-finite retained-return panel after the structural first-row handling.

\code{ledgr_validation_pbo_invalid_threshold} is raised when a PBO/CSCV threshold
is not a finite numeric scalar.

\code{ledgr_validation_min_trl_invalid_reference} is raised when a minimum track
record length request supplies an invalid reference Sharpe ratio.

\code{ledgr_validation_min_trl_invalid_confidence} is raised when a minimum track
record length request supplies a confidence level outside \verb{(0, 1)}.

\code{ledgr_validation_min_trl_invalid_risk_free} is raised when a minimum track
record length request supplies an invalid per-period risk-free return.

\code{ledgr_validation_min_trl_too_few_observations} is raised when minimum track
record length has too few post-first-row observations.

\code{ledgr_validation_min_trl_invalid_returns} is raised when minimum track
record length receives non-finite or constant retained returns.

\code{ledgr_validation_k_ratio_invalid_periods_per_year} is raised when a K-Ratio
request omits or supplies an invalid expected observations-per-year value.

\code{ledgr_validation_k_ratio_invalid_risk_free} is raised when K-Ratio receives
an invalid per-period risk-free return.

\code{ledgr_validation_k_ratio_too_few_observations} is raised when K-Ratio has
fewer than three return observations.

\code{ledgr_validation_k_ratio_invalid_returns} is raised when K-Ratio receives
non-finite returns, an excess return at or below \code{-1}, or a cumulative
log-wealth path whose slope standard error is zero or non-finite.

\code{ledgr_validation_cluster_invalid_threshold} is raised when retained-return
clustering receives an invalid correlation-distance threshold.

\code{ledgr_validation_cluster_too_few_candidates} is raised when retained-return
clustering has fewer than two completed candidates.

\code{ledgr_validation_cluster_too_few_observations} is raised when retained-return
clustering has too few post-first-row observations.

\code{ledgr_validation_cluster_invalid_returns} is raised when retained-return
clustering receives non-finite or constant retained returns.

\code{ledgr_validation_dsr_invalid_effective_trials} is raised when DSR receives
an invalid effective independent trial count.

\code{ledgr_validation_dsr_too_few_candidates} is raised when DSR has fewer than
two completed candidates.

\code{ledgr_validation_dsr_invalid_confidence} is raised when DSR receives a
confidence level outside \verb{(0, 1)}.

\code{ledgr_validation_dsr_invalid_risk_free} is raised when DSR receives an
invalid per-period risk-free return.

\code{ledgr_validation_dsr_too_few_observations} is raised when DSR has too few
post-first-row observations.

\code{ledgr_validation_dsr_invalid_returns} is raised when DSR receives
non-finite, constant, or otherwise unsupported retained returns.
}

\section{Business-objective classes}{

\code{ledgr_invalid_business_objective} is raised when an objective is empty or
does not have the required classed, serialized, all-pass shape.

\code{ledgr_duplicate_objective_criterion} is raised when an objective contains
duplicate criterion ids.

\code{ledgr_business_objective_hash_mismatch} is raised when an objective's
canonical plan JSON or hash does not match its criterion steps.

\code{ledgr_invalid_objective_criterion} is raised when a criterion is unclassed,
malformed, or has invalid parameters. \code{ledgr_unknown_objective_criterion}
is raised for criterion ids that ledgr does not own in v1.

\code{ledgr_objective_non_serializable_params} is raised when criterion
parameters cannot be represented by the canonical objective plan.
\code{ledgr_objective_criterion_hash_mismatch} is raised when a criterion hash
does not match its serialized payload.

\code{ledgr_invalid_objective_verdict} is raised when an internal criterion
evaluator returns a malformed verdict. \code{ledgr_objective_missing_evidence},
\code{ledgr_objective_non_finite_evidence}, and
\code{ledgr_objective_invalid_evidence} fail closed on unusable criterion input.

\code{ledgr_invalid_diagnostic_threshold} is raised for unsupported diagnostic
result classes, columns, comparisons, or malformed embedded evidence.
\code{ledgr_diagnostic_source_hash_mismatch} is raised when an embedded
diagnostic snapshot does not match its source hash.

\code{ledgr_stable_region_invalid_min_neighbors} is raised for an invalid
support-neighbor threshold. \code{ledgr_stable_region_invalid_grid} and
\code{ledgr_stable_region_invalid_metric} cover malformed lattice or score input.
More specific lattice classes are \code{ledgr_stable_region_unordered_axis},
\code{ledgr_stable_region_unsupported_axis}, \code{ledgr_stable_region_collapsed_axis},
\code{ledgr_stable_region_duplicate_tuple},
\code{ledgr_stable_region_incomplete_grid}, and
\code{ledgr_stable_region_no_adjacent_pairs}.

\code{ledgr_invalid_sweep_filter_input} and
\code{ledgr_sweep_filter_no_completed_candidates} cover malformed or empty
sweep-filter inputs. \code{ledgr_sweep_filter_diagnostic_source_mismatch} is
raised when embedded diagnostic evidence came from a different return
panel. \code{ledgr_sweep_filter_parameter_missing} and
\code{ledgr_sweep_filter_ambiguous_parameter} cover strict-lattice parameter
extraction failures. \code{ledgr_invalid_sweep_filter_result} covers malformed
filter evidence. \code{ledgr_sweep_filter_not_candidate},
\code{ledgr_sweep_filter_promotion_forbidden}, and
\code{ledgr_sweep_filter_walk_forward_forbidden} explicitly prevent the
all-candidates evidence result from entering selection surfaces; all three
inherit from \code{ledgr_sweep_filter_evidence_only}.

\code{ledgr_missing_package} is raised when a public optional-package adapter is
requested but the package is not installed.
}

\section{Metric-context warning classes}{

\code{ledgr_metric_context_cadence_mismatch} is emitted when a daily metric
context is applied to evidence whose observed median interval is clearly
subdaily. The warning identifies a possible annualization mismatch; it does
not change metric values, metric recipes, stored evidence, or identity.
}

\section{Walk-forward classes}{

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_metric_missing} is raised when a selection rule requests
a metric column that is absent from the train-window score rows.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_metric_class_invalid} is raised when a selection metric
is not classified as valid for v1 scalar selection.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_no_selection} is raised when all candidate values for the
requested selection metric are missing, \code{NA}, \code{NaN}, or infinite. Inside
\code{ledgr_walk_forward()} it ends the session only under
\code{no_selection = "fail"}; the default \code{"previous"} reuses the latest
training selection, or runs no test window before the first one.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_gapped_carry} (also
\code{ledgr_walk_forward_invalid_fold_window}) is raised by
\code{ledgr_walk_forward()} under \code{opening_state_policy = "carry_test_state"}
when a pulse lies between two consecutive test windows, before any work
runs. Its message names the first gap; use contiguous folds or
\code{"flat_test_state"}.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_overlapping_carry} (also
\code{ledgr_walk_forward_invalid_fold_window}) is raised by
\code{ledgr_walk_forward()} under \code{opening_state_policy = "carry_test_state"}
when a test window does not start after the previous one ends (overlap or
reverse order), before any work runs. Its message names the first such pair;
use contiguous folds or \code{"flat_test_state"}.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_candidate_key_missing} is raised when the train-window
score rows passed to a selection rule do not include a \code{candidate_key} column.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_test_run_failed} is raised when a selected test run
cannot produce a usable test score row.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_session_not_found} is raised when walk-forward
inspection helpers cannot find the requested session.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_snapshot_hash_mismatch} is raised when the supplied
snapshot does not match the persisted walk-forward session identity.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_snapshot_override_mismatch} is raised when an explicit
snapshot override for candidate extraction has a different \code{snapshot_id} or
\code{snapshot_hash} than the walk-forward result locator.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_invalid_session} is raised when persisted walk-forward
session rows, linked test runs, or identity fields cannot be reopened
safely.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_latest_without_rationale} is raised when extracting
\code{fold_seq = "latest"} without an explicit \code{selection_rationale}.

\code{ledgr_walk_forward_candidate_not_found} is raised when a requested
walk-forward fold does not contain a completed selected candidate.
}

\section{Availability reason codes}{

Availability-aware diagnostics use this closed vocabulary. An accepted fill
without a complication uses an empty reason code.\tabular{lll}{
   Exact token \tab Stage \tab Action / interpretation \cr
   \code{decision_recorded} \tab decision \tab unrestricted decision recorded \cr
   \code{empty_public_domain} \tab decision \tab empty axis; no targets emitted \cr
   \code{trading_halted} \tab restriction \tab hold or exit only \cr
   \code{quotation_only} \tab restriction \tab hold or exit only \cr
   \code{status_unknown} \tab restriction \tab hold or exit only \cr
   \code{status_unknown_or_conflicting} \tab restriction \tab hold or exit only \cr
   \code{lifetime_inactive} \tab restriction / terminal \tab hold or exit until the terminal resolves under the declared policy \cr
   \code{stale_mark_reduction} \tab risk \tab reducing target accepted with a stale mark \cr
   \code{stale_mark_pass_through} \tab risk \tab unchanged target accepted with a stale mark \cr
   \code{risk_mark_unavailable} \tab risk stop \tab accepted prefix finalized incomplete \cr
   \code{restricted_target} \tab target validation \tab classed strategy-result failure \cr
   \code{nonmember_exposure_increase} \tab target validation \tab classed strategy-result failure \cr
   \code{post_risk_inadmissible} \tab post-risk validation \tab classed risk failure \cr
   \code{short_exposure_unsupported} \tab target validation \tab classed strategy-result failure \cr
   \code{insufficient_cash} \tab execution \tab cash-consuming fill rejected \cr
   \code{execution_bar_missing} \tab execution \tab no fill; no standing order \cr
   \code{membership_changed_before_execution} \tab execution diagnostic \tab report only; never an execution gate \cr
   \code{final_pulse_no_execution} \tab execution \tab no fill without a later pulse \cr
   \code{affordability_reconciled} \tab reconciliation \tab accepted fills applied and reconciled \cr
   \code{affordability_reconciliation_failed} \tab reconciliation stop \tab accepted prefix finalized incomplete \cr
   \code{valuation_horizon_exhausted} \tab valuation stop \tab under \code{exhausted = "refuse"}, or a holding with no mark at all; accepted prefix finalized incomplete \cr
   \code{valuation_frozen} \tab valuation / restriction \tab under \code{exhausted = "freeze"}, carried at its last close; hold or exit only, no transaction \cr
   \code{valuation_freeze_exited} \tab valuation diagnostic \tab a frozen holding resumed, was exited or was disposed \cr
   \code{terminal_disposition} \tab valuation \tab modeled terminal outcome posted as one \code{DISPOSITION} before the strategy decision \cr
   \code{terminal_settlement_unsupported} \tab valuation stop \tab unlabeled or refused terminal; holding preserved, no fabricated settlement \cr
   \code{terminal_mark_unavailable} \tab valuation stop \tab the terminal choice needs a mark that does not exist; accepted prefix finalized incomplete \cr
   \code{corporate_action_cash_refused} \tab valuation stop \tab a held corporate-action cash settlement refused by policy; accepted prefix finalized incomplete \cr
   \code{corporate_action_quantity_refused} \tab valuation stop \tab a held quantity effect, unmodeled fact or refused (\code{complete = FALSE}) fact refused by policy; accepted prefix finalized incomplete \cr
   \code{fold_exception} \tab error \tab failed after transaction rollback \cr
}


For the connected workflow and interpretation, see
\code{vignette("survivorship-bias", package = "ledgr")} and
\code{system.file("doc", "survivorship-bias.html", package = "ledgr")}.
}

\section{Evidence, assumptions and refusals}{

Availability-aware results keep six cases apart.
\itemize{
\item \strong{Settlement evidence.} A supported settlement fact or a scheduled
corporate-action row disposes a holding as recorded. It is evidence, not
an assumption, and it pre-empts every modeled choice.
\item \strong{Modeled terminal disposition} (\code{terminal_disposition}). A labeled
\code{known_inactive} holding without settlement evidence is disposed under the
declared \code{held_terminal_position} choice. The result names the choice and
whether it was declared or a default, for example
\verb{default: assumed worthless}.
\item \strong{Stale valuation} (\code{stale_close}). A holding is valued at a close no
older than \code{max_sessions}. Cash and quantity stay exact.
\item \strong{Frozen valuation} (\code{valuation_frozen}, \code{frozen_close}). Under
\code{exhausted = "freeze"} a holding is carried at its last close beyond
\code{max_sessions}. Cash and quantity stay exact, but equity during the freeze
is an assumption-backed estimate, not an exact value.
\item \strong{Refusal.} \code{valuation_horizon_exhausted},
\code{terminal_settlement_unsupported}, \code{terminal_mark_unavailable},
\code{corporate_action_cash_refused} and \code{corporate_action_quantity_refused}
stop the run \code{INCOMPLETE} and keep the accepted prefix. Nothing is
fabricated. A dense run has no typed stop: its corporate-action refusals
raise \code{ledgr_corporate_action_unsupported}.
\item \strong{Frozen-at-end bound.} \code{total_return_if_frozen_worthless} in
\code{\link[=ledgr_valuation_summary]{ledgr_valuation_summary()}} restates endpoint return with holdings still
frozen at the end valued at zero. It is a bound, not a corrected return,
Sharpe ratio or drawdown.
}
}

